   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leaving No One Behind: Helping Countries to Report on SDG Indicators by Migratory Status - PHASE II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There are several direct references to migration in the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development (2030 Agenda). Migration is also a cross-cutting theme relevant to most 2030 Agenda Goals (SDGs). While the inclusion of migration in the 2030 Agenda is a key opportunity, it also presents countries with a series of new data challenges and reporting requirements, as large amounts of new migration data are required for monitoring of progress against the SDGs. However, relevant data frameworks have not yet risen to these challenges. One specific challenge is the need to disaggregate indicators by migratory status. In 2021 IOM&#x2019;s Global Migration Data Analysis Centre, with the support of Statistics Sweden, developed a dedicated guide to help practitioners disaggregate data by migratory status. There is now an opportunity to encourage and support use of this guide in selected pilot countries in Africa, building on existing capacity building partnerships and activities in the region. The objectives of this programme of work are to assist two to four pilot countries in Africa to disaggregate SDG-related and other development data by migratory status, and to showcase progress in migratory status disaggregation in pilot countries and encourage peer-to-peer learning and knowledge exchange.</narrative>
  </description>
